                        "language": "english",
                        "review": "[b]picture builder[/b] has you constructing images from overlapping tetris blocks, can't just place them over emptiness. it's jigsaw mixed with a hint of perspective-based shenanigans, as you have to figure out what to cover with what and in what order.\n\nthe [b]56 images[/b] can be played in 6 different ways, essentially offering [b]336 levels[/b], all unlocked from the start, but there are [b]only 2 main modes, both with 3 difficulty choices[/b]. according to the store page, there are alternate solutions for some levels, which I guess is fine in something like this, whatever works.\n\n[u]mosaic[/u] on [i]easy[/i] offers single-tile pieces and a full outline of the target in the playing area (those are the tiles other pieces can be placed on), so it's coloring by numbers but without the numbers, not much point to it and it's beyond tedious to drag dozens or hundreds of pieces one by one (though coloring by numbers is tedium personified anyway). [i]medium[/i] has tetris pieces with a full outline and [i]hard[/i] also provides tetris pieces, but only a few random tiles to put pieces on. these levels don't utilize overlap.\n\n[u]3d mode[/u] is the real meat of the game (though mosaic hard can be tricky too), with tetris pieces covering more than the actual real estate, so overlapping is essential. pieces can be moved and removed freely, as long as nothing is covering them.\n\nthere's a 'how to play' section explaining the basics and the non-rebindable controls. hold left click to drag pieces, right click or 'r' to rotate, esc for the menu, that's all you need really. though I wouldn't mind if mouse wheel switched between available shapes, making dragging optional.\n\n[b]there are absolutely no settings[/b] or icons to click while playing a level. the presentation is fine otherwise and alt+enter makes a resizable window, but come the fuck on. an even bigger issue and a dealbreaker on its own is [b]the lack of mid-level saving[/b]. it'd also be nice if level select showed picture size as well.\n\n[b]half price would be more appropriate if it had any sort of basic functionality, until then obviously don't bother[/b]. there's a [b]demo to try[/b] to see if you like the concept though. I do, even if it's not something my brain can comprehend, so it'd be great if the developer put some more work into it to make it recommendable.",
